    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs can offer personalized tutoring, explain concepts in simple language, and generate practice problems tailored to a student’s level. They can support diverse learning styles and reduce anxiety by being patient and non-judgmental. In classrooms, they could assist teachers with lesson planning or provide instant feedback. This makes math more accessible and engaging for all students."
